    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Correlation, Confounding & Causality\"\ndescription: \"See how association emerges, how confounders create misleading patterns, and why prediction and causal explanation are different goals.\"\nauthor: \"MLStation\"\ndate: 2026-10-01\ncategories: [Statistics, Correlation, Causality, Data Science]\ndraft: false\n---\n\n\nTwo variables moving together is useful information.\n\nIt is not automatically a causal story.\n\n::: {.callout-tip}\n## What you will learn\n- Covariance and Pearson correlation\n- Why correlation measures linear association\n- Confounding and Simpson's paradox\n- Prediction versus causal inference\n- Why feature importance is not causal effect\n:::\n\n## Correlation\n\nPearson correlation is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)}{s_Xs_Y},\n$$\n\nwith $-1\\le r\\le1$.\n\nIt measures **linear** association.\n\n## Interactive: rotate the correlation cloud\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\nviewof rho = Inputs.range([-.95,.95], {value:.6, step:.05, label:\"Correlation ρ\"})\nrr=d3.randomLcg(.41)\nnormal=()=>{let u=rr()||1e-9,v=rr(); return Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(u))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*v)}\ncloud=d3.range(600).map(()=>{let x=normal(),e=normal();return{x,y:rho*x+Math.sqrt(1-rho*rho)*e}})\nPlot.plot({\n height:360,x:{domain:[-4,4]},y:{domain:[-4,4]},\n marks:[Plot.dot(cloud,{x:\"x\",y:\"y\",r:3,fill:\"#4F46E5\",fillOpacity:.45}),Plot.ruleX([0]),Plot.ruleY([0])]\n})\n```\n\n## Confounding: a third variable changes the story\n\nImagine ice-cream sales and drowning incidents both rise in summer.\n\n```text\nTemperature\n  ↙      ↘\nIce cream   Swimming exposure\n               ↓\n            Drowning\n```\n\nThe association between ice cream and drowning does not imply that buying ice cream causes drowning.\n\n## Simulation: Simpson's paradox\n\n::: {#fcaf8274 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code code-fold=\"true\"}\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\n\nrng=np.random.default_rng(33)\nrows=[]\nfor group,offset,xmu in [(\"A\",5,1),(\"B\",-5,5)]:\n    x=rng.normal(xmu,.8,180)\n    y=.8*x+offset+rng.normal(0,.7,180)\n    rows += [{\"x\":a,\"y\":b,\"group\":group} for a,b in zip(x,y)]\ndf=pd.DataFrame(rows)\nfig=px.scatter(df,x=\"x\",y=\"y\",color=\"group\",trendline=\"ols\")\nfig.update_layout(height=390)\nfig.show()\nprint(\"Overall correlation:\",df[[\"x\",\"y\"]].corr().iloc[0,1])\nprint(df.groupby(\"group\").apply(lambda g:g[[\"x\",\"y\"]].corr().iloc[0,1]))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:390px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"60b2ecc7-d341-4c2e-a116-f5b3f1ff9b7a\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"60b2ecc7-d341-4c2e-a116-f5b3f1ff9b7a\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"60b2ecc7-d341-4c2e-a116-f5b3f1ff9b7a\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"group=A\\u003cbr\\u003ex=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003ey=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"A\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#636efa\",\"symbol\":\"circle\"},\"mode\":\"markers\",\"name\":\"A\",\"orientation\":\"v\",\"showlegend\":true,\"x\":{\"dtype\":\"f8\",\"bdata\":\"kiwO82AZ9T\\u002fZkjwhe5fhP7ScTo1+ifc\\u002fM0G8OQOK8D8+fiN3G27Qv7xrpOc40vw\\u002fZ0iVAY9+7T\\u002fnjyfG9+73P2WLcD53wQNAkmOBYZdv8z8l0ITFcvnBPzur2b9FI